1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,900
You type SIX words, hit Enter, and a whole website APPEARS. Here's the journey behind that.

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:10,700
First, your browser has to FIND
where that DOMAIN actually points.

3
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:15,500
It asks DNS for the right ADDRESS, like
looking up a contact before calling.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,900
Next, your browser opens a
CONNECTION to that SERVER.

5
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:23,900
For a SECURE site, it also sets
up an ENCRYPTED HTTPS connection.

6
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:27,500
Then it sends a REQUEST:
please give me this PAGE.

7
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:35,400
The server replies with data: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, IMAGES, or links to more files.

8
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:39,300
Your browser reads those pieces
and BUILDS the PAGE you see.

9
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:44,700
That is why a page can look BROKEN while the server responds fine: one image failed to load.

10
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:49,300
So the short version: FIND the address,
connect, request, receive, RENDER.

11
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:54,000
Next time you type a URL,
you'll see the whole JOURNEY.
